# Solution note

Start every question `.cpp` with one line that states the task, not the algorithm. Skip `templates/main.cpp`. Skip a file that already starts with the question.

```cpp
// Question: Merge sorted nums2 into sorted nums1 in place.
```

After the code, add this note. Skip a file that already contains `Time Complexity:`. Fill the note from the code in that file.

```cpp
// Time Complexity: O(n)
// Space Complexity: O(1)
// Pattern: Two Pointers - From End to Start
// explanation:
/*
one short paragraph of the actual moves in this file.
name the leftover case or the state, when there is one.
*/
```

- Time and space use the variables from that problem. A sort is `O(n log n)`. A DP table states both dimensions.
- Pattern names the branch and the variant.
- The explanation describes this file. Do not repeat a sentence, and do not change the code above the note.

When a file is added under `leetcode-150/`, also update `leetcode-150/patterns/`. Add the question under the pattern it uses. If the idea is new, create the next numbered pattern file and one row in `patterns/README.md`.
